node_modules
# Keep environment variables out of version control
.env

/generated/prisma

# LOCAL-FIRST (2026-08-19): the SQLite database itself. This is DATA, not code.
#
# Before this change the database lived in a Postgres container and there was
# nothing in the repo folder to accidentally commit. Now it's a plain file at
# prisma/dev.db, sitting right next to the schema — and `git add -A` would
# happily commit it.
#
# Three reasons that must never happen:
#   - It holds real guest records. Names, phone numbers, dates of birth. Once
#     Mississauga is live, committing it publishes customer data into git
#     history, where deleting it later is genuinely hard.
#   - Every site has its OWN database. They are not meant to agree, and two
#     sites pushing theirs would conflict on every single commit.
#   - It's a binary that changes on every sale, so each commit would carry a
#     fresh copy of the whole file.
#
# The migrations in prisma/migrations/ ARE code and DO belong in git — they're
# the instructions for building an empty database. The database is what those
# instructions produce locally.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
